# 43. Real-World JSON API Example

Imagine a cybersecurity API returns:

```json
{
    "ip": "192.168.1.10",
    "status": "suspicious",
    "risk_score": 85
}
```

Python can process it:

```python
import json

response = '''
{
    "ip": "192.168.1.10",
    "status": "suspicious",
    "risk_score": 85
}
'''

data = json.loads(response)

print("IP:", data["ip"])
print("Status:", data["status"])
print("Risk Score:", data["risk_score"])
```

Output:

```text
IP: 192.168.1.10
Status: suspicious
Risk Score: 85
```

This is similar to how security automation tools process API responses.

